# Brand spelling: Petrozz

The product brand is **Petrozz** (two z’s, one t).

- Always write **Petrozz**, never **Pettroz**
- Apply this in UI copy, headings, CTAs, metadata, docs, comments, and new content
- Correct casing variants the same way: `Petrozz`, not `Pettroz` / `PETTROZ` → `PETROZZ` when all-caps is required
- Do not introduce “Pettroz” in code strings, content files, or user-facing text

Exception: do not rename existing repo/path/package/CSS identifiers (for example `pettroz-landing`, `/pettroz-bl.svg`, `.pettroz-mega-item`) or live domains (`pettroz.in`) unless explicitly asked. Env vars may keep legacy `PETTROZ_*` aliases alongside `PETROZZ_*`.
